{"q":"3247","t":"Number of Subsequences with Odd Sum","d":"Medium","p":true,"c":null,"h":["Define <code>dp[i][0]</code> as the answer for the subarray <code>[0, i]</code>.","Similarly define <code>dp[i][1]</code> as the answer for the subarray <code>[0, i]</code> if we wanted to count even-sum subsequences.","If <code>nums[i]</code> is odd, <code>dp[i][x] = 2<sup>i</sup></code>.","Otherwise, <code>dp[i][x] = dp[i - 1][x] * 2</code>.","<code>dp[0][1] = 1</code> if <code>nums[0]</code> is odd, and 0 otherwise.","<code>dp[0][0] = 2</code> if <code>nums[0]</code> is even, and 1 otherwise (since an empty subsequence has an even sum)."],"m":"{\n  \"name\": \"subsequenceCount\",\n  \"params\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"nums\",\n      \"type\": \"integer[]\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"return\": {\n    \"type\": \"integer\"\n  }\n}","g":[{"name":"Array","slug":"array"},{"name":"Math","slug":"math"},{"name":"Dynamic Programming","slug":"dynamic-programming"},{"name":"Combinatorics","slug":"combinatorics"}]}